From 794b7110e6f2f629a4071ef701fc152a6410ef0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:47:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] rutabaga_gfx: route virglrenderer's log into the VMM
 log by level

rutabaga installed virglrenderer's deprecated level-less debug callback and
logged everything at debug!, so a VMM at the default warn level never showed
why Venus marked a guest ring fatal (vkr logs the reason at INFO, then the
guest driver aborts with 'abort on fatal').

Install virgl_set_log_callback instead: DEBUG -> debug!, INFO and WARNING ->
warn!, ERROR -> error!. The level-aware callback also bypasses
virglrenderer's own VIRGL_LOG_LEVEL filter, so nothing is dropped before it
reaches the log.
---
 src/rutabaga_gfx/src/virgl_renderer.rs | 56 +++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rutabaga_gfx/src/virgl_renderer.rs b/src/rutabaga_gfx/src/virgl_renderer.rs
index 56142c9..1e4db66 100644
--- a/src/rutabaga_gfx/src/virgl_renderer.rs
+++ b/src/rutabaga_gfx/src/virgl_renderer.rs
